{"name":"Aqua Sky","hex":"#70bbbf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/1280px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cirriform clouds and a quarter Moon in the blue daytime sky over Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASky_over_Munich_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/